    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1113">

                <pb facs="0805" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.48/1877a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Consul General Hanna.</hi><anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d1113-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 25, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>As the reasons which influenced this Government heretofore to furnish assistance
                    and transportation to American citizens in Mexico <pb facs="0806" n="690"
                        xml:id="pg690"/> appear to exist no longer, you are instructed to decline
                    hereafter all such applications. So inform all Consuls in your district.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1113-f1" n="93" type="source" xml:id="d1113-f1-content">
                <p>Same to Consul Canada at Vera Cruz with instruction to, repeat to Consul at
                    Tampico.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
